# `vectispire-angular/openapi.json` was here, as a build artefact of the NestJS era: it was
# generated locally and nobody kept it. It is now the committed contract of every route, and
# `ClientContractSpecTest` fails when the code and the file disagree — ignoring it would mean the
# test asks for a file the repository refuses to hold, which is a red build on every checkout.

# macOS
.DS_Store


# Gradle build output for the JVM port
vectispire-java/**/build/
vectispire-java/**/.gradle/
# Kotlin's incremental-compilation state for the buildSrc scripts.
vectispire-java/**/.kotlin/
**/bin/**
*.class

# Playwright test artifacts & reports
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
vectispire-angular/test-results/
vectispire-angular/playwright-report/
vectispire-angular/blob-report/
vectispire-angular/.playwright/

# Gradle's CI-local home. It was appended to a file with no trailing newline and
# spent 43 commits glued to the line above, ignoring nothing.
.gradle-ci/

# This machine's worktrees and session state. `.claude/agents/` is exempt: it is
# tracked, shared, and `.claude/**` would have hidden the next agent added to it.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/

# L'environnement Python et la build locale du site de documentation.
/.venv/
# La build locale du site de documentation (mkdocs build / mkdocs serve).
/site/

# Le fichier de connexion déléguée porte un secret client : il reste local.
.env.oidc

# La configuration IntelliJ de cette machine. IntelliJ écrit son propre `.idea/.gitignore`,
# mais il n'exclut que ce qu'il sait volatil — `workspace.xml`, les sources de données — et
# laisse committer le reste : des chemins de SDK et de runners qui n'existent que sur le poste
# qui les a écrits, et qui cassent l'import chez le suivant plutôt que de l'aider.
.idea/

# npm's own state when HOME points here (the update notifier's timestamp was committed once).
/.npm/
